 "notes": "Blind pass P1/A. Orientation: P1370687 and P1370700 are single pages photographed rotated (read after a 90° clockwise rotation); P1370701 is upright, single page (continuation of the P1370700 postscript: it begins \"entiere\", and closes with the date \"le 4e 7bre 1651\" and the signature \"Louis de Bourbon\"). No bifolium, so there are only L labels. Multi-line clear runs carry the label of their first line: P1370687 L12 = one line; P1370700 L16 = closing formula, date and signature block (3-4 lines), L17 = 6-line postscript, all clear; P1370701 L1 = lines 1-5 up to \"de\", L9 clear = lines 9-13 with the date and signature.\nSymbol decisions: the open cup with a vertical stem through it, which looks like a cursive 4 (single-glyph tokens after \"que\", in \"34.ψ.19\", \"66.ψ.82\", etc.) = SYM:psi throughout. pi = short low \"π\" with splayed legs; Pi = taller \"TT\" with long legs (P1370687 L2 is uncertain between the two). P1370687 L6 has an \"I\"-like sign with a top serif and a long base bar, transcribed as SYM:T-renversé?. P1370700 L10 and the bottom insertion have a small closed loop with a long stroke rising from its top and curving right, transcribed as SYM:sigma? (alternative: single-digit 6|tilde). P1370687 L14 has a normal single \"6\" with a detached tick at upper right, transcribed as 6|acute?. P1370700 L11 has a token like \"a\" fused with a w/psi stroke (\"aw\"), transcribed as SYM:autre-a+w-ligature? (possibly a correction).\nSingle digits: P1370687 L16 \"1\" (one dot above) and \"2\" (two dots) are separate tokens, given as 1|diaeresis? and 2|diaeresis. P1370687 L12 \"11\": one dot over each 1, given as 11|diaeresis?.\nInsertions and corrections in P1370700: (a) a left-margin insertion \"+35.ψ.38.26.33.32.69.63.45.76.\" is written beside the struck-out start of L9, and a \"+\" also stands in the right margin after L8. It is placed between L8 and L9 as its own run (labelled L9 with an insertion field). (b) The struck-out text at the start of L9 (cipher-like \"x.4?.gx8\", illegible) and the struck-out clear word(s) after \"31.\" in L9 are cancelled and NOT tokenised. (c) A line written below \"Cependant\" (labelled L14) starts with \"‡\", and the matching \"‡\" is in the right margin at the end of L9, so the run sits right after L9's last token (18|macron) and before L10. A long signature flourish crosses this line (over psi/20/96), and the readings under it are still fairly sure. (d) In L10, \"19\" seems to be written over another figure (the 9 has an extra lower stroke), given as 19|tilde?. (e) Two dots just before \"69\" at the start of L11 lie on the archive stamp border and are ignored.\nP1370687: the interlined \"ff\" in \"fortifications\" (L12) is a clear-text correction. Stray dots/ink spots are ignored.\nP1370701: line 4 \"affe\" has a sign like \"8\" under the ff, and line 5 starts with a sign like \"8\" with superscript \"lo\" before \"ont faict\". This is probably an abbreviation for \"affe(ctio)ns\" / \"qu'ils\", put in the clear text with a '?' and not tokenised; check it.\nModern annotations are not transcribed as letter text: pencil \"1651\" and \"2 E 1841/18 .3\" with \"M. Duchaubon?\" (P1370687); \"2E 1841/18 - 10\" and \"M. Duchaubon?\" (P1370700); archive stamps. Date on P1370700: \"De Paris? le 3e septembre 1651\" (place uncertain).\nFaint diaeresis dots on P1370700 (lighter ink) are the main uncertainty: 63/33/69/76/19 are given as diaeresis?.\n"
